---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Enterprise | Griffith Creative"
  description="Rebuilds, migrations, and ongoing management for high-traffic sites and the companies behind them. Griffith Creative, Los Angeles, working worldwide."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container-site hero-grid">
      <p class="eyebrow">Enterprise</p>
      <div class="hero-body">
        <h1 class="h1">Built to hold under load.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          When traffic spikes and the deadline does not move, everything has to hold. We audit, rebuild, and manage the infrastructure&nbsp;behind&nbsp;it.
        </p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-primary">Book a call</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-site">
      <div class="stacked">
        <h2 class="h2">What we take on</h2>
        <p class="para">
          A rebuild of the site, a migration off whatever it runs on now, and management once it is live. Peak load is the design target: launches, press, seasonal demand, live events. The senior people who build it stay on it afterwards, through ongoing development, content operations, monitoring,&nbsp;and&nbsp;security&nbsp;patching.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-site pair">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="sub-head">The audit</h2>
        <p class="col-para">
          Old platforms accumulate cost the way they accumulate tech debt: hosting contracts, redundant delivery layers, extended support for end-of-life software, and licenses for services you stopped using years ago. We map every contract, license, and dependency and show you what each one is for, before&nbsp;anything&nbsp;is&nbsp;rebuilt.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="sub-head">The rebuild</h2>
        <p class="col-para">
          Static-first architecture served from a global edge network, faster under load and more secure by default. Your data relationships, your measurement, and your content library come across with it. End-of-life software, unpatched dependencies, and accessibility gaps are closed as part of&nbsp;the&nbsp;work.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-site two-col">
      <h2 class="h2">Systems</h2>
      <p class="para">
        Most companies run on systems nobody chose. We sit with your team, learn how the work really happens, and rebuild the storage, software, and workflows around it. <a href="/systems/" class="text-link">More&nbsp;on&nbsp;Systems</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-site">
      <p class="statement">
        Uptime and performance monitoring on every site we manage. Performance measured before launch and after. Every saving from a systems rebuild checked against the&nbsp;invoices&nbsp;afterwards.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-close">
    <div class="container-site close">
      <div class="close-main">
        <h2 class="h2-close">Start with the audit.</h2>
        <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-primary">Book a call</a>
      </div>
      <div class="close-next">
        <a href="/systems/" class="next-link">Systems</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
